## What changed

The defect (verified at HEAD before editing): ShellHook::pre_execute matched Ok((code, _)), discarding the hook's stderr — the exact String run_command builds for it (stderr(Stdio::piped()) → cap_hook_stderr; stdout is Stdio::null()). So echo 'run cargo fmt first' >&2; exit 3 rendered as only Pre-hook 'pre:bash' exited with code 3. The load-bearing half is the audience: maybe_hook wraps that Err(String) into ToolError::Failed(format!("Blocked by hook: {reason}")) — it is what the agent reads one turn later.

`src/hooks.rs`
• New pure pre_hook_block_message(name, code, stderr) beside cap_hook_stderr. It neither caps nor slices — the cap already happened char-boundary-safely upstream, and a &stderr[..n] here would be #250 again (the doc comment says so at the call site).
• The one blocking arm now binds and passes the stderr.
• One sentence added to hook_phase_teaching_lines() — as an addition; the shared-closing-facts guard is untouched and green.

`src/help_data.rs` — the matching sentence in command_help("hooks"), inserted after the existing Pre-hooks that exit non-zero block… line, nothing reworded.

Tests (added, none edited)
• `pre_hook_block_message_table — whole-string assert_eq!` over 6 rows, including the two byte-identical rows that are the entire regression surface (`("", 1, ...)` and `("   \n\t", 7, ...)`), plus `✓` and em-dash rows with anti-vacuous fixture assertions so a later byte-indexing regression reddens there.
• `blocking_pre_hook_reports_its_stderr` — behavioural through the real `HookRegistry` + real `ShellHook`, with its **near-miss twin**: a bare `exit 3` hook must produce *exactly* `Pre-hook 'pre:bash' exited with code 3, via assert_eq!`.

`tests/module_size.rs` — register pasted from what the gate printed: ("src/hooks.rs", 3684) (was 3545; +139, past the 100-line grace band, so fatal until pasted).

`ARCHITECTURE.md` — the hooks.rs entry got its Day-209 history paragraph.

