## Out of scope, named
Exit-code contract unchanged (non-zero still blocks — I did not adopt Claude Code's "only exit 2 blocks" semantics, which would widen what existing hooks permit); Err(e) spawn path untouched; the Blocked by hook:  prefix stays. Stated limit: this makes the hook's reason reach the model; it does not make a silently-blocking hook say anything, and no cap was added here since the stderr is already bounded upstream.
